makehuman2  project notes:
    1. opengl/camera.py     line 235 handles camera zoom 
    2. opengl/camera.py     line 381 handles camera rotation rotation(xAngle, yAngle)
            > Horizontal rotation (lines 395-397): Rotates the camera position around the cameraDir (up axis) using xAngle
            > Vertical rotation (lines 401-403): Rotates the resulting position around the rightVector using yAngle
            > Angles come from arcBallRotation (line 304-305): xAngle = (last_mousex - x) * deltaAngleX, yAngle = (last_mousey - y) * deltaAngleY
            > deltaAngleX = 2π / viewport_width, deltaAngleY = π / viewport_height (lines 419-420) — so a full drag across the screen = full 360° horizontal / 180° vertical rotation


